        "body": "Closes #6847\n\n## Problem\n\n`PlexIntegration.getMediaReleasesAsync()` only reads `/library/recentlyAdded`, which returns **seasons** with the season's own `addedAt`. Episodes added to a season that already exists never change that value, so the media releases widget never shows them (the widget looks stale for anyone following ongoing shows).\n\n## Change\n\n- Additionally fetch the most recently added episodes of every `show` library (`/library/sections/{id}/all?type=4&sort=addedAt:desc`, one request per show library, 50 items each).\n- Seasons already in `/library/recentlyAdded` that received newer episodes are bumped to the episode's `addedAt` and use its `originallyAvailableAt` as release date.\n- Seasons that fell out of `/library/recentlyAdded` but got new episodes are rebuilt from the episode metadata (`grandparentTitle` / `parentTitle`, `grandparentThumb` + `art` as images, link to the season).\n- Result is sorted by `addedAt` desc and capped at 50 (Plex's default page size), so the widget behaves like Plex's own \"Recently added\" and like the Jellyfin integration (`Items/Latest` groups episodes into their series).\n- Any failure while fetching episodes is logged and falls back to the previous behaviour, so servers/tokens without library access are unaffected.\n- Small refactor: `fetchJsonAsync()` helper shared by the JSON endpoints, `recentlyAddedItemSchema` extracted so it can be reused.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Existing spec unchanged and passing (episode fetch fails in its mock \u2192 fallback path).\n- New spec: bumped season ordering + release date, season rebuilt from episode metadata (title, images, href), and fallback when the episode endpoints error.\n\n`pnpm --filter @homarr/integrations typecheck`, `lint` and `vitest run packages/integrations/src/plex` pass.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Plex recently added content now includes the latest episodes for each show.\n  - Seasons missing from Plex\u2019s recent-items list can now be recovered from episode information.\n  - Season dates and ordering reflect the newest available episode, with results limited to the 50 most recent items.\n  - Season detail links now use cleaner, more reliable URLs.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Plex integrations now gracefully fall back to the available recent-items data when episode details cannot be retrieved.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
